Package: claude-scheduler
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: systemd
Recommends: awscli, libnotify-bin
Homepage: https://github.com/raulsh/claude-scheduler
Description: Scheduled Claude Code tasks with dependency healthchecks
 claude-scheduler runs Claude Code (the claude CLI) on a cron schedule behind
 a local web UI, streaming each run's output live and keeping its history.
 .
 Before every execution it checks the dependencies that task declared - AWS
 CLI profile logins, MCP server status, required binaries - and refuses to run
 against a broken environment rather than burning tokens on a dead
 credential. Failures raise a desktop notification.
 .
 The claude CLI itself is not packaged for Debian and therefore cannot be a
 dependency. Install it separately; the service reports a clear warning until
 it is found.
